    "tune": "public domain: traditional (French, 18th century), printed long before 1931",
    "arrangement": "original, written for Stackapella (our own voicing; the 1919 book's harmony used only to check the chords: some of its editors died less than 70 years ago)",
    "recordings": "synthesized guides",
    "checked": null,
    "source": "\"For He's a Jolly Good Fellow!\", No. 61 in Peter W. Dykema, Will Earhart, Osbourne McConathy and Hollis Dann, eds., Twice 55 Community Songs, No. 1: The Brown Book (Boston: C. C. Birchard, copyright 1919), archive.org/details/twice55community01dyke (leaf n38), the verse ending \"which nobody can deny!\", G major 6/8, its melody (the top of the printed chords) note for note, down a whole step to F, in 6/8 as printed; no fermatas; the last \"ny!\" held to the bar's end; checked against Louis C. Elson, Folk Songs of Many Nations (Cincinnati: John Church, 1905), p. 52, archive.org/details/bub_gb_FCvaAAAAMAAJ (leaf n57), the same tune in G 6/8, whose verse ends \"So say we all of us\" and whose pickups are two sixteenths"
